  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showery conditions today through Saturday.\nAreas of fog this morning which could be locally dense.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nSurface low pressure exits across the Maritimes today, with a \ntrof extending back across the forecast area, while an upper \nlow begins to move south across the region. Showers will persist\nacross the region today, with the better chances across \nnorthern areas. Could also have the slight chance of an \nafternoon thunderstorm. The surface/upper lows vertically stack \nacross the Maritimes tonight into Saturday, slowing the movement\nof the system. A disturbance moving around the Maritimes system\nwill rotate across the region Saturday. Shower chances will \npersist tonight into Saturday. The system then exits Saturday \nnight into Sunday. Additional rain totals today through Saturday\nwill generally range from a tenth up to around a quarter of an \ninch. Abundant low level moisture will support areas of fog \nthis morning which could be locally dense.",
